  {
   "index": 8,
   "tag": "p",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 491,
   "text": "Despite the fact that DeAngelis and Marcucci provided Fabian with singing lessons, his career did not take off right away. His first single, “I’m in Love,” met with little but critical derision when it was released. But the proprietors of Chancellor were unwilling to give up; they stirred up massive amounts of publicity about Fabian, and booked him for an East Coast tour of many theaters and audit",
